## 3. Coding Standards

### General Rules
- Always use **Vue 3 Composition API** with `<script setup>` — never Options API
- Always use **Tailwind CSS** utility classes — never write custom CSS unless absolutely required
- All backend logic lives in **Services** — controllers must be thin (receive request, call service, return Inertia response)
- All form validation lives in **FormRequest** classes — never validate in controllers directly
- Use **API Resources** (`php artisan make:resource`) for all data passed to Inertia pages
- Never pass raw Eloquent models to Inertia — always pass through a Resource
- Use **route model binding** everywhere (`{product:slug}` not `{id}`)
- All routes use **named routes** — never hardcode URLs in Vue components, always use Inertia `route()` helper
- Use `ziggy-js` for route generation in Vue components

### Vue Component Rules
- One component per file
- Component file names: **PascalCase** (e.g. `ProductCard.vue`)
- Page file names: **PascalCase** matching the route (e.g. `Products/Index.vue`)
- Props must always be typed using `defineProps<{}>()` TypeScript syntax
- Emits must always be typed using `defineEmits<{}>()` TypeScript syntax
- Use `useForm()` from `@inertiajs/vue3` for ALL form submissions — never use raw `axios.post`
- Use `<Link>` from `@inertiajs/vue3` for ALL internal navigation — never use `<a href>`

### Laravel Rules
- Controllers return `Inertia::render()` or `redirect()->route()`— nothing else
- Use `$request->validated()` always — never `$request->all()`
- All models use `$fillable` — never `$guarded = []`
- Soft deletes on: Products, Categories, Orders, Users
- All migrations include `timestamps()` and where relevant `softDeletes()`
- Use Laravel Policies for all authorization — never check roles inline in controllers
- Use `php artisan make:policy` for each model

