## 4. User Roles & Permissions

| Role | Description |
|---|---|
| `super_admin` | Full unrestricted access. Can manage all admins, site settings, and every feature. |
| `admin` | Scoped access based on assigned permissions. Cannot manage other admins or site settings unless explicitly granted. |
| `user` | Public customer. Can browse, order, review, and manage their own account. |

### Permission Scopes (for admin role)
Each permission is a boolean column or JSON field on the admin user record:

| Scope | Actions |
|---|---|
| Products | view, create, edit, delete, manage_stock |
| Categories | view, create, edit, delete |
| Attributes | view, create, edit, delete |
| Orders | view, update_status, refund |
| Reviews | view, approve, delete, respond |
| Customers | view, edit, export |
| Promo Codes | view, create, delete |
| Site Settings | view, edit |
| Admin Users | super_admin only — not grantable to admin role |

### Role Enforcement
- `App\Http\Middleware\AdminMiddleware` — checks `auth()->user()->role` is `admin` or `super_admin`
- `App\Http\Middleware\SuperAdminMiddleware` — checks role is `super_admin` only
- Use Laravel Policies for model-level authorization
- In Vue: use shared Inertia prop `$page.props.auth.user.role` to show/hide UI elements

